  "summary_en": "Japan's Road Transport Vehicle Act (1951, current revision effective 2026-04-01) governs vehicle registration, safety standards, inspection, maintenance and certification. It covers automated driving devices (Art. 41), requires ministerial permission for program-altering modifications such as over-the-air updates (Art. 99-3), and sets penalties.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Vehicles must meet safety and environmental standards (保安基準) before operation (Arts. 40-46).",
   "Art. 41(2) defines 自動運行装置 (automated driving system) replacing the driver's cognition, judgment and operation, with data-recording device.",
   "Art. 99-3 requires MLIT permission for specified modifications via program/software changes, including over-the-air.",
   "Type designation, inspection, and recall-type corrective measure notifications for manufacturers (Arts. 63-2 to 63-4, 75).",
   "Designated maintenance providers are certified; Chapter 8 sets criminal penalties for violations."
  ],
